    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Big Music is the sixteenth studio album by Simple Minds, released in 2014 on Caroline International. It marked the band’s first album of new material in over five years and was presented as a return to form, with a sound that draws on electronic textures, rock dynamics, and pop hooks while revisiting the widescreen style that made the group famous.\n\nThe album balances muscular, arena-sized arrangements with bright synth lines and anthemic choruses, giving songs like “Honest Town,” “Blindfolded,” and “Midnight Walking” a strong melodic push. It was issued in standard and deluxe formats, including a bonus-disc edition with extra tracks and covers, and it was well received as a late-period statement that reconnects Simple Minds with their classic blend of new wave, pop, and rock energy.",
